{
  "_comment": [
    "The command menu the map opens on a unit, plus the shield line on the",
    "unit-ability screen.  These are pool strings in bank $D2: each one is",
    "pointed to individually, so a string that outgrows its slot is moved and",
    "repointed rather than truncated.",
    "",
    "The menu box is 24 pixels of text -- three 8x16 cells, measured off the",
    "highlight band, which is the same width in the clean ROM.  The kanji it was",
    "built for are 12px each, so two of them fill it exactly.  The entries are",
    "spelled with the game's own font rather than the Thai page because fixed",
    "cells keep the menu's relative line break working with no padding, and the",
    "price is that only A-Z, 0-9 and space exist there and only three of them",
    "fit.  The build refuses a fourth letter rather than let it draw on the",
    "frame's own column.",
    "",
    "The shield line is not in that box and has no relative break after it, so it",
    "stays on the Thai page and is free to be as wide as it reads best."
  ],
